Book a MAC makeup appointment now.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSwiss bubble-car maker cries foul over incentives limited to large EVs (https://www.ft.com/content/05b244a9-fbf2-4a0d-b243-0b6298ad82a1)\nciteturn757news54 [wordlim: 100] Published: 6 months ago; Wim Ouboter, founder of Micro Mobility Systems and creator of the Microlino electric \"bubble car\", is challenging Swiss carbon trading regulations for excluding his compact vehicle from emissions incentives. Although designed to reduce urban emissions, the Microlino—a retro-style microcar modeled after the 1950s Isetta and built in Italy—is categorized as a \"motorcycle\" instead of a \"passenger car\" under Swiss law. This categorization disqualifies it from participating in Switzerland's carbon credit scheme, which financially benefits larger EV manufacturers like Tesla. Ouboter contends the rules are skewed in favor of big manufacturers and warns he might move production to China, where he has offers of financial support. Micro has asked for a formal ruling from Swiss authorities and, represented by prominent lawyer Cordelia Bähr, plans to fight the case in court, with possible escalation to EU platforms. Priced between €15,000 and €22,000, the Microlino suits short urban trips and embodies sustainable mobility. The dispute highlights a broader European debate over whether current climate policies unjustly favor larger electric vehicles over smaller, more eco-efficient options.\nSwiss bubble-car maker cries foul over incentives limited to large EVs\nDate: Tue Apr 14 04:00:07 2026 UTC\n\nThe entrepreneur behind the Micro scooter craze that took the world by storm is taking on the Swiss government over climate benefits that exclude his latest venture - the Microlino electric \"bubble car\". \nWim Ouboter is contesting Switzerland's carbon trading regulations, arguing they unfairly exclude his two-seat electric vehicle from a system that financially benefits larger global rivals such as Tesla.\nLaunched in 2022 by Ouboter's Micro Mobility Systems, the Microlino is an electric microcar inspired by the 1950s classic Italian Isetta and built in Turin, the historic heart of Italy's car industry.\nMicro, which generates roughly SFr70mn ($87mn) in annual turnover, has ploughed profits from its scooter business into the bubble cars, several thousand of which have been sold across Europe.\nAt the heart of the dispute is a technical distinction. Only vehicles classified as \"passenger cars\" are included in Switzerland's emissions system, under which importers of petrol vehicles buy carbon credits from EV companies to meet fleet emissions targets. \n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nEstée Lauder | Up to 25% Off Your Order* (https://www.esteelauder.com/)\nciteturn757view0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://www.esteelauder.com/\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 159\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nAMARA Home & Living | Chăn Ga Gối Nệm Khách Sạn 5 Sao (https://amarahome.vn/)\nciteturn757view1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://amarahome.vn/\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 267\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nInternal Error ()\nciteturn757view2 [wordlim: 200] Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://www.pullandbear.com/vn/man/shoes/see-all-n6414\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 1\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nĐường (https://winmart.vn/duong--c01151)\nciteturn757view3 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://winmart.vn/duong--c01151\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 7\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nInternal Error 